Hello and happy holidays to you and yours.

My research partner and I have a simple question regarding the results of a Bayesian CFA we performed in blavaan to compare model fit statistics of a multidimensional scale.

We were able to obtain fit measures successfully (the results appear to have converged without any errors) save for the marginal log likelihood which says “-Inf”, and we are unsure how to interpret this result.

I am afraid to say that we are relatively new to SEM/CFA and have struggled mightily with traditional CFA approaches that perpetually state that our data generates a not-positive definite matrix, so to see that Blavaan could go smoothly is a welcome sign of progress. Are we mistaken, and in fact this is definitely a big problem? Any insights or advice would be greatly appreciated.

Thank you for your time.

